  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="e679-ee11-37aa-c30b" name="Gothic and Vandal Kingdoms (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #54 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). These largely Germanic tribes overran large areas of the Western Roman Empire, often after initially being invited to settle as Federates within the Empire’s boundaries. Their success proved transitory and several of their kingdoms were conquered by the Byzantines. The Visigoths in Southern Spain held on until overrun by the Arab expansion in 720 AD, and the Lombards until defeated by the Byzantines in 1018 AD. The list can be used to construct Vandal, Visigoth, Ostrogoth and Lombard armies. 

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Gothic and Vandal Kingdoms - Lombard Armies]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: Up to 50% Elite Warriors cannot be taken; Warriors are Light Infantry with hand weapon and composite bow, and are Ld6 at 10 points each. Cavalry: Up to 66% Elite Cavalry may have First Charge (+5). Allies: Up to 20%: Avars (Steppe Nomad list) Characters and Elite Cavalry must be armed with thrusting spears and should take heavy armour.
[Gothic and Vandal Kingdoms - Ostrogoth Armies]
  Cavalry: up to 66%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: Up to 50% Warriors may be Light Infantry with hand weapon and composite bow, at 8 points each. Cavalry: Up to 66% Comitatus and warrior cavalry may take barding (+4). Allies: Up to 20%: Up to 2 units of Berber cavalry or Byzantine Foederati from the Early Byzantine Cavalry or Light Cavalry units.
[Gothic and Vandal Kingdoms - Vandal Armies]
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 20%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: Up to 20% Cavalry: At least 50% Allies: Up to 20%: Up to 2 units of Berber cavalry from the Early Byzantine list. Vandal cavalry are Light Cavalry with Feigned Flight (+3). They may not take javelins, and troops indicated in the list to be armed with Mixed Weapons must take throwing spears instead (+1).
[Gothic and Vandal Kingdoms - Visigoth Armies]
  Cavalry: up to 66%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 33%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: Up to 33% Cavalry: Up to 66% Elite Cavalry may have First Charge (+5). Allies: up to two Berber cavalry, or Byzantine light cavalry from the Early Byzantine list.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
